leap-chorus takes its runtime architecture from orca: the daemon/client split, PTY
ownership by a detached versioned daemon, NDJSON framing over a unix socket, and
the `@xterm/headless` emulator-per-pane approach. Files deriving from orca name it
in a header comment.
